<Base title="PYQ guide" description="How to use GATE previous-year questions effectively: topic-wise solving, error tagging and official sources." canonicalPath="/guides/pyq-guide/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">Method</p><h1>PYQ guide</h1><p class="lead">PYQs show real difficulty and recurring ideas — but only when solved topic-wise, timed later, and reviewed honestly.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid cols-2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Method</h3><ol><li>Finish a topic, then solve its PYQs untimed.</li><li>Tag each question: concept / formula / trick / lengthy.</li><li>Re-solve misses after 7 days.</li><li>Later: year-wise timed sets.</li><li>Log everything in the <a href="/tools/mistake-tracker/">mistake tracker</a>.</li></ol></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Sources</h3><p>Prefer official papers. This site links rather than republishes where rights are unclear. <a href="/pyq/">Open PYQ navigation →</a></p></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
